---
import BaseHead from '../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title="Validated RAG Eval Harness | Ravikumar Buragapu"
			description="A human-validated harness for measuring LLM-as-judge agreement on RAG answers and citation support."
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<p>RAG RESEARCH · EVALUATION · HUMAN VALIDATION</p>
			<h1>Validated RAG Eval Harness</h1>
			<p>
				Does LLM-as-judge agree with human reviewers on RAG answer
				correctness and citation support? Compare naive, rubric-based,
				and stepwise judge prompts against independent human labels.
			</p>

			<section aria-labelledby="measures">
				<h2 id="measures">Measure agreement—not just model scores</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>Three-class answer labels: correct, partially correct, or wrong.</li>
					<li>Separate binary judgments for whether cited passages support the answer.</li>
					<li>Nominal Cohen's κ, raw agreement, confusion counts, and per-type disagreements.</li>
					<li>Judge cost from provider token usage and optional human labor cost.</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					Human labels are blank until reviewers complete them.
					The included 50-case fixture is illustrative and cannot
					establish agreement or represent multi-hop, numeric, or
					negation question performance.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="run">
				<h2 id="run">Prepare independent human labels first</h2>
				<pre><code>cd rag-judge-eval
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e ".[dev]"
pytest
rag-judge-eval prepare
# Complete results/human-review.csv before seeing judge outputs.
export OPENAI_API_KEY="..."
rag-judge-eval run --model gpt-4o-mini</code></pre>
				<p>
					<a href="https://github.com/buragapuravi/my_research_work/tree/main/rag-judge-eval"
						>Read the project README</a
					>
					·
					<a href="/projects/chunking-ablation">Explore Chunking Strategy Ablation</a>
				</p>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
